Images and embedded media
-------------------------

Topic pages and curriculum covers reference images hosted elsewhere. No image
from these hosts is redistributed in this repository; each is fetched by the
reader's browser at view time. Licensing follows the host, per file.

Wikimedia Commons
  upload.wikimedia.org, commons.wikimedia.org
  The largest source of illustrative imagery in this project, used heavily
  throughout the History curriculum and in several Mathematics topics. Each
  file on Commons carries its own license (public domain, CC BY, CC BY-SA, and
  others) and its own attribution requirements.

  Attribution is carried in the page itself, not in this file. Every figure
  that displays a Commons image states the licence in its caption and links
  to the file's description page on Commons, which names the author and the
  exact licence version. This holds for all 74 such figures.

  If you reuse one of these images outside this project, take the terms from
  the Commons file page. Do not rely on this notice.
  https://commons.wikimedia.org/

Open Library Covers API
  covers.openlibrary.org
  Book cover images. Open Library is a project of the Internet Archive.
  https://openlibrary.org/dev/docs/api/covers

Google Books
  books.google.com
  Book cover thumbnails, used as a fallback when Open Library has no cover.

YouTube
  i.ytimg.com (video thumbnails), www.youtube-nocookie.com (embedded player)
  Thumbnails and embeds for the video topics. The privacy-enhanced
  youtube-nocookie.com domain is used for embeds. Thumbnails and embeds remain
  the property of YouTube and the respective video creators.
  See src/components/home/curriculum-view.jsx and
  src/components/learning/learning-mode.jsx.

No film imagery is used anywhere in this project. The Star Wars film analysis
is written commentary only. Its visualizations are drawn from measurements and
plot structure, not from stills: the ship comparison renders each vehicle as a
bar whose width is its true length against a meter ruler, and the character
roster is set in type.

Earlier versions displayed studio and fan-wiki photographs under a claim of
fair use. Those were removed so that nothing in this project depends on a
fair-use defence. Every asset now loads under an explicit licence, is in the
public domain, or is original work.

